- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #5: 'ServerError and Unauthorized Display impls pass\
    \ through raw server body text \u2014 CWE-209 risk' and notes the security test\
    \ is a no-op. Partially caught \u2014 flags CWE-209 on error Display but focuses\
    \ on server error variants rather than the eprintln path specifically."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer finding #4: 'SiemClient uses raw String for tenant_id instead\
    \ of TenantId newtype \u2014 client.rs:11' explicitly flags that axiathon-core\
    \ exports TenantId but SiemClient stores Option<String>, bypassing type safety."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that 6 dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on ClientConfig. Reviewer\
    \ verified this in finding #12: 'deny_unknown_fields on ClientConfig \u2014 unknown\
    \ TOML keys (including token) are rejected at config.rs:29.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'The specific vacuously-true assertion pattern (is_none() || ...) was
    not flagged. Reviewer finding #6 catches a different weak assertion pattern (if
    let Ok), and finding #7 catches a different vacuous test, but neither addresses
    the is_none() || true pattern from I5.'
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase flagged the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic with
    ''let _ = config''. Reviewer finding #7 is about a different test (config_file_does_not_store_tokens),
    not the default config test with zero assertions.'
